<title>HONDURAS: Honduras April inflation 0.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Honduras April inflation 0.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TEGUCIGALPA, Honduras 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Honduras' consumer price index rose 0.6 percent in April, the lowest monthly increase since 1994, the central bank said on Friday.</p>
<p>Accumulated inflation for the year was 5.9 percent, compared to an accumulated rate of 7.1 percent during the same period the year before.</p>
<p>The government predicts a year-end inflation rate of 16 percent, a goal analysts said was acheivable.</p>
<p>The year-on-year inflation rate as of April was 24 percent.</p>
<p>((--Gustavo Palencia, Tegucigalpa bureau (502) 32-78-98))</p>
